"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1KFDNVSDZ1S0QA39\",\"title\":\"DMS Georgia — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"VALIDATED\",\"BICRS\",\"1,000Y+\",\"DMS Georgia\",\"Rewind\",\"ISSUED\",\"108.92\",\"BUFFER POOL\",\"5.453\",\"CREDITING PERIOD\",\"01 Mar 2025 to 01 Mar 2030\",\"Summary\"],\"issued_header\":\"108.92\",\"buffer_header\":\"5.453\",\"crediting\":\"01 Mar 2025 to 01 Mar 2030\",\"verifier\":\"Normec Verifavia\",\"code\":\"J1AM\",\"approval\":\"01 May 2026\",\"protocol_current\":\"Subsurface Biomass Carbon Removal and Storage v1.1\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":\"108.92\",\"cert_retired\":\"60\",\"cert_buffer\":\"5.453\",\"reversal\":\"The risk of reversal for this project has been assessed as low. This means that 5% of certificates issued for this project are allocated to Rewind's buffer pool.\\n\\nTo date, this project has contributed 5.453 certificates to the buffer pool which holds a total of 5.453 certificates.\\n\\nRewind has no reversals to date.\",\"showing\":[\"Showing 1 of 1\",\"Showing 4 of 4\",\"Showing 1 of 1\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Name\",\"Category\",\"Validated\"],\"rows\":[[\"Sawdust from GTA Georgia\",\"Biomass\",\"28 Apr 2026\"]]},{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"01 May 2026\",\"Validation and Verification Report\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"01 May 2026\",\"GHG Statement Report\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"01 May 2026\",\"Public Comment Period Summary\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"31 Mar 2026\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"]]},{\"heads\":[\"Issue date\",\"Issued\",\"Buffer pool\",\"Supplier allocation\"],\"rows\":[[\"01 May 2026\",\"108.92\",\"5.453\",\"103.467\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1HXGZ55MM1S0XRBC\",\"t\":\"Rewind\"},{\"h\":\"https://normecverifavia.com\",\"t\":\"Normec Verifavia\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/subsurface-biomass/1.1\",\"t\":\"Subsurface Biomass Carbon Removal and Storage v1.1\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1HXGZ55MM1S0XRBC/prj_1KFDNVSDZ1S0QA39/pjd_1KQHJ00K11S0PR5P/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"Project Design Document | 31 Mar 2026\"},{\"h\":\"/ghg-entry/rmv_1KMNQWSCN1S05GNS?tab=calculation-view\",\"t\":\"See GHG entry →\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1HXGZ55MM1S0XRBC/prj_1KFDNVSDZ1S0QA39/pjd_1KQYTZNM21S02Q1Q/validation_and_verification_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1HXGZ55MM1S0XRBC/prj_1KFDNVSDZ1S0QA39/pjd_1KQHJF34G1S05BMA/ghg_statement_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1HXGZ55MM1S0XRBC/prj_1KFDNVSDZ1S0QA39/pjd_1KQHJ5V3C1S0AD1B/public_comment_period_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1HXGZ55MM1S0XRBC/prj_1KFDNVSDZ1S0QA39/pjd_1KQHJ00K11S0PR5P/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"VALIDATED\\nBICRS\\n1,000Y+\\nDMS Georgia\\nRewind\\nISSUED\\n108.92\\nBUFFER POOL\\n5.453\\nCREDITING PERIOD\\n01 Mar 2025 to 01 Mar 2030\\nSummary\\nRemoval method\\nCalculation overview\\nFeedstocks\\nProject documentation\\nCertificates\\nReversal risk\\nSummary\\n\\nThe project achieves carbon removal by storing biomass in sealed, underground chambers of a coal mine, preventing decomposition and long-term CO₂ release. Sawmill residues (sawdust) are collected, transported, and securely deposited underground. These chambers provide a stable, oxygen-limited environment that ensures permanent carbon sequestration. By repurposing abandoned coal infrastructure for carbon storage, the project effectively offsets emissions while preventing biomass decomposition products from re-entering the carbon cycle.\\n\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nCurrent verifier\\nNormec Verifavia\\n->\\nProject code\\nJ1AM\\nApproval date\\n01 May 2026\\nCurrent protocol version\\nSubsurface Biomass Carbon Removal and Storage v1.1\\nSUSTAINABLE DEVELOPMENT GOALS\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nDMS Georgia\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nProject Design Document\\n31 Mar 2026\\nCalculation overview\\nCalculations demonstrating 4.10 tCO₂e removed from DMS Georgia on 31 Jul 2025\\nSee GHG entry →\\nNet CO₂e Removed\\n4.104 t\\nSequestrations\\n4.551 t\\n-\\nActivities\\n310 kgCO₂e\\n-\\nUncertainty Discount\\n137 kg\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nView full screen\\nFeedstocks\\n\\nFeedstocks are the validated input materials that have been used for this project.\\n\\nName\\tCategory\\tValidated\\nSawdust from GTA Georgia\\tBiomass\\t28 Apr 2026\\nShowing 1 of 1\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n01 May 2026\\tValidation and Verification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n01 May 2026\\tGHG Statement Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n01 May 2026\\tPublic Comment Period Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n31 Mar 2026\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 4 of 4\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nCertificates\\nIssued\\n108.92\\nRetired\\n60\\nBuffer pool\\n5.453\\nCrediting period\\n01 Mar 2025 to 01 Mar 2030\\nIssuances\\nRetirements\\nIssue date\\tIssued\\tBuffer pool\\tSupplier allocation\\n01 May 2026\\t108.92\\t5.453\\t103.467\\nShowing 1 of 1\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nReversal risk\\n\\nThe risk of reversal for this project has been assessed as low. This means that 5% of certificates issued for this project are allocated to Rewind's buffer pool.\\n\\nTo date, this project has contributed 5.453 certificates to the buffer pool which holds a total of 5.453 certificates.\\n\\nRewind has no reversals to date.\\n\\nLearn more about reversal risk\"}"